WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.130
Your lungs could have
been two simple balloons.

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:08.070
Instead, each lung is packed with
tiny air sacs called alveoli,

3
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.110
bunched together like grapes.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.390
Breathe in, and air
rushes down into them.

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.890
Breathe out, and it rushes back up.

6
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.550
Why build a lung out of
so many tiny bubbles,

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.750
instead of one big bag?

8
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.490
In this mission, you'll follow
oxygen and carbon dioxide as

9
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.640
they move by diffusion
between the air and the blood.

10
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:32.250
You'll find out what makes alveoli
such good exchange surfaces.

11
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.350
And you'll see how the diaphragm
and the intercostal muscles

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.870
between your ribs move air in and out.

13
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.810
Your mission: explain why your
lungs are built from tiny air

14
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:43.950
sacs.
